  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "On current version of VRCSDK for Avatars (3.4.0-beta1), I must fix the issues with shaders and PhysBone hard limits before I can click the \"Build & Publish\" button to upload a Quest avatar.\n\nHowever, with Editor scripts hooked into avatar building, a PC avatar on Scene could theoretically be uploaded as Quest compatible one, not only fixing shaders and PhysBones issues but doing various optimizations on the fly.\n\nCurrently this workflow is impossible because I cannot click the \"Build & Publish\" button to initiate any optimization magic if there looks like any issues in shaders and PhysBones, even if they would be resolved on build process.\n\nIn particular, shaders and PhysBone hard limits for Quest avatars should be enforced AFTER avatar preprocessing, and not on the VRCSDK control panel. Some warning could be shown if a Quest  avatar upload would likely fail, but should not block the Build button.",
